  "concepts": [
    {
      "id": "TR-IV-EVENT",
      "title": {
        "en": "Direction is only one price driver"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Diagnose the illustrative option loss using price drivers and the desk comparison rule."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] of a bought option reflects more than the direction of the index. The [[T-TR-IV]] is inferred from the option price through a pricing model."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-payoff"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "In this illustrative case, [[T-TR-IV]] fell from 17.5% to 11% after the announcement. That [[T-TR-CRUSH]] and elapsed time outweighed the favourable index move; direction alone did not protect the [[T-TR-PREMIUM]]. The desk uses the [[T-TR-STRADDLE]] as a rough [[T-TR-MOVE]] guide, not a guaranteed range or a profit threshold."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §2, EV-2.1; scenario marketBefore, marketAfter, impliedMove, decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-payoff"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "The case [[T-TR-STRADDLE]] costs 153.55 plus 150.75, giving an [[T-TR-MOVE]] guide of 304.30 points. The desk rule EV-2.1 asks a historical note to compare its expected move with the [[T-TR-MOVE]]. In the replay, record the [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] drivers and the missing comparison before assessing the decision."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §2, EV-2.1; scenario marketBefore, marketAfter, impliedMove, decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-payoff"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] can fall even when the index moves favourably. Keep the desk [[T-TR-MOVE]] heuristic separate from the model price and the realised outcome."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §2, EV-2.1; scenario marketBefore, marketAfter, impliedMove, decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-IV-EVENT-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-payoff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-THETA",
      "title": {
        "en": "Separate waiting from the IV change"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Use a controlled repricing comparison to identify the cost of waiting in the case."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-TR-THETA]] of an option describes model sensitivity to a day passing with other inputs fixed. The [[T-TR-TIME]] is the [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] above intrinsic value."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Theta",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-iv-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "A fall in [[T-TR-IV]] and the passage of time are different drivers of [[T-TR-PREMIUM]]. The case attribution assigns about 23 rupees per unit to time, with separate volatility and spot contributions. The [[T-TR-THETA]] is a local sensitivity, so multiplying its entry value by several days need not give an exact repricing."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §3, EV-3.1; scenario bsCheck and decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Theta",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-iv-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "The desk rule EV-3.1 asks for a one-day-later [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] at the same spot before a historical overnight hold. Keep [[T-TR-IV]] and the other model inputs fixed to isolate waiting in that comparison. Save the replay inputs beside the [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] comparison so a reviewer can reproduce the reasoning."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §3, EV-3.1; scenario bsCheck and decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Theta",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-iv-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "A change in [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] across a night is not automatically all [[T-TR-THETA]]. Label a controlled time-only comparison separately from a full-case attribution."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §3, EV-3.1; scenario bsCheck and decomposition"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-THETA-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Theta",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-iv-line"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-EVENT-RISK",
      "title": {
        "en": "Size the risk before judging the result"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Calculate the illustrative budget and evaluate the old position against its maximum loss."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-TR-BUDGET]] is the illustrative desk limit on [[T-TR-LOSS]] for an event trade. A [[T-TR-DEFINED]] structure still needs sizing; a bounded loss can exceed the [[T-TR-BUDGET]]."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, EV-4.1 to EV-4.5; scenario context and sizing"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-risk-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "Under the desk rule EV-4.1, the [[T-TR-BUDGET]] is 1% of the 1000000-rupee paper book, or 10000 rupees. The case long option puts the full [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] at risk before fees, with no claim about current exchange specifications. The realised loss was 9210 rupees, but the [[T-TR-LOSS]] at entry was 27075 rupees, so sizing breached the rule."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, EV-4.1 to EV-4.5; scenario context and sizing"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-risk-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "At the case [[T-TR-PREMIUM]] of 90.25 and 75 units per lot, [[T-TR-LOSS]] per lot is 6768.75 rupees before charges. The desk rule EV-4.2 rounds the budget divided by [[T-TR-LOSS]] per lot down to whole lots. The replay calculation permits 1 such lot before costs, rather than the historical 4; record the breach without placing an order."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, EV-4.1 to EV-4.5; scenario context and sizing"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-risk-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "Judge the [[T-TR-BUDGET]] against [[T-TR-LOSS]] at entry, separately from the eventual outcome. Document [[T-TR-DEFINED]], position size and stress assumptions in the historical review."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, EV-4.1 to EV-4.5; scenario context and sizing"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-EVENT-RISK-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-risk-flow"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "TR-PRETRADE",
      "title": {
        "en": "Review the decision separately from its P&L"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Write an auditable historical note and separate process quality from the result."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "A [[T-TR-NOTE]] records the thesis, priced move, structure, [[T-TR-LOSS]], exit plan and invalidation before the paper order. The [[T-TR-BIAS]] appears when a result replaces a review of the original reasoning."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, EV-6.1; trainee checklist; scenario trade.preTradeNote"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-note-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "The desk rule EV-6.1 requires process and outcome to be tagged separately. A profitable result does not repair a missing [[T-TR-NOTE]] or an [[T-TR-BUDGET]] breach. The case note named direction but omitted the [[T-TR-MOVE]], [[T-TR-LOSS]] and exit plan."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, EV-6.1; trainee checklist; scenario trade.preTradeNote"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-note-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "For the historical review, reconstruct what the [[T-TR-NOTE]] lacked and mark reconstructed fields as hindsight. Use the original information to explain the move comparison and the [[T-TR-BUDGET]] breach. Write a short process finding and a separate outcome line; do not fabricate an exit plan that never existed."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, EV-6.1; trainee checklist; scenario trade.preTradeNote"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-note-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "A [[T-TR-NOTE]] is an entry-time record, not a story rewritten after the outcome. Counter [[T-TR-BIAS]] by naming the rule and evidence before describing the profit or loss."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Options desk playbook: event days (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, EV-6.1; trainee checklist; scenario trade.preTradeNote"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-CASE",
              "title": "Historical paper option case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/trader/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-TR-PRETRADE-OIC",
              "title": "Options Industry Council: Volatility and the Greeks",
              "locator": "Opened 2026-11-20; model sensitivities and assumptions"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "tr-note-flow"
        }
      ]
    }
